<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helen Clark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helen Clark is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> politician who was Prime Minister from 1999 to 2008, leading the Fifth Labour Government through three terms. She was the first woman elected Prime Minister at a general election. Her government kept New Zealand out of the 2003 invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and maintained low unemployment. From 2009 to 2017 she was Administrator of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Development Programme.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helen-clark.jpg" alt="Helen Clark" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Global Commission on Drug Policy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Helen_Clark_official_photo_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
